+### R8 · MCP spec 2026-07-28 (stateless, OAuth 2.1 + PKCE, HTTP semantics) — `accept_verbatim`
+
+**What changed:** the spec makes MCP stateless, standardizes OAuth 2.1 with PKCE, and
+converges on plain HTTP semantics — moving MCP from developer convention to enterprise
+infrastructure (Trilogy analysis, 2026-07-23).
+
+- **Pros:** stateless servers eliminate an entire class of session-state bugs and scale
+  horizontally — directly relevant to the Control Tower's Render deployment; OAuth 2.1
+  + PKCE is exactly the zero-credential-to-credential bridge our slot architecture
+  needs; protocol-standard alignment keeps SupremeAI interoperable with Claude, Cursor,
+  Gemini, ChatGPT, and VS Code clients instead of bespoke adapters.
+- **Cons:** migration cost: our tower currently issues session IDs on initialize;
+  stateless mode changes heartbeat, lease, and HITL-approval flows that assume
+  session affinity; spec compliance without capability negotiation can break older
+  clients.
+- **Risks:** half-migrated state (some adapters stateful, some stateless) is worse than
+  either extreme; OAuth flows in autonomous agent lanes must never auto-approve.
+- **Anti-patterns flagged:** hand-rolled auth beside a standardized OAuth path;
+  long-lived sessions holding implicit trust.
+- **এটা করা যাবে না:** no adoption that silently drops the fail-closed property of slot
+  authorization, and no OAuth grant flows that bypass Human-In-The-Loop approval for
+  admin-scope tools.
+- **SupremeAI adoption path:** the one verbatim-accept item this cycle — rfc to adopt
+  the spec baseline across tower adapters (Issue P-02), gated behind HITL review.
+
+### R9 · ALMA — Automated meta-Learning of Memory designs for Agentic systems — `adapt_cleanroom`
+
+**What it is (Clune group, Feb 2026 per papers-of-week):** a meta-learning approach that
+automatically searches over memory architecture designs for agents rather than fixing
+one (episodic vs long-term vs RAG vs graph).
+
+- **Pros:** SupremeAI's memory sidecar already runs all these substrates (episodic
+  records, learned facts, vector store, knowledge graph) — ALMA says the *router*
+  between them should be learned from win-rates, not hand-coded; cheap to prototype
+  with existing memory_get_similar_tasks feedback as the reward signal.
+- **Cons:** meta-learning loops need eval volume we may not have yet; a mis-learned
+  router degrades every downstream agent at once — a single point of silent failure.
+- **Risks:** optimizing memory retrieval for benchmark tasks that don't match real
+  cadence work; feedback loops that reinforce stale routing.
+- **Anti-patterns flagged:** learning-based routing without a deterministic fallback.
+- **এটা করা যাবে না:** no learned router in the autonomous lane without a manual
+  override and a per-route accuracy floor; never train the router on tenant-private
+  content.
+- **SupremeAI adoption path:** clean-room — start with measured win-rate tracking per
+  memory route (Issue P-04); automate selection only after baselines exist.
+
