+## 3b. Cross-Cutting Anti-Patterns Observed This Cycle
+
+1. **Tier theater** — flagship/mid/budget naming used to justify flagship-everything routing.
+2. **Spend-blind upgrade** — model bumps adopted on benchmark deltas within noise (<1 pt).
+3. **Green-test illusion** — passing tests mistaken for production integration (Muse Wonder).
+4. **Churn blindness** — new versions burning 1.7–2.6x tokens/churn without gates (Fable 5.1, Astra xhigh).
+5. **Open-washing** — "open later, some pieces proprietary" consuming community labor (Muse Spark).
+6. **Floating aliases** — evals/pins on "latest" instead of exact versions (Gemini cadence).
+7. **Charters without controls** — governance prose without enforceable mechanisms.
+8. **Always-on without ledgers** — persistent agents with no budget or kill-switch (dot pattern).
+9. **Paper-driven rewrites** — infra changes from papers without own profiling (DualPath).
+10. **Silent vendor policy shifts** — cyber-capable model availability changing under political pressure.
